NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table is a headless table library. It manages your table's state and logic (sorting, filtering, pagination, selection, and more) while you keep 100% control over the markup and styles. This page gets you from install to a rendering Angular table, then shows how to layer on your first feature."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/angular-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"your-first-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your First Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component and template below are complete. Drop them into an Angular app and you will see a working table."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// app.ts\nimport { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { FlexRender, injectTable, tableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// 1. Define the shape of your data\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}\n\n// 2. Create some data with a stable reference\nconst defaultData: Array<Person> = [\n  { firstName: 'tanner', lastName: 'linsley', age: 24 },\n  { firstName: 'tandy', lastName: 'miller', age: 40 },\n  { firstName: 'joe', lastName: 'dirte', age: 45 },\n]\n\n// 3. New in v9: declare which features this table uses (none yet)\nconst features = tableFeatures({})\n\n// 4. Define your columns\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = [\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'firstName', // accessorKey shorthand\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorFn: (row) => row.lastName, // accessorFn alternative with a custom id\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue<string>(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'age',\n    header: () => 'Age',\n  },\n]\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  imports: [FlexRender],\n  templateUrl: './app.html',\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n})\nexport class App {\n  // 5. Own the data with a signal so updates flow into the table\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  // 6. Create the table instance\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table', // registers this table with the devtools\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- app.html -->\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th>\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A few things to note:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures({})"},{"type":"text","value":" declares which optional features the table uses. Registering only what you need keeps bundles small and gives TypeScript accurate types for the table instance."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" must be called in an injection context. Its initializer re-runs when Angular signals read inside it change (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this.data()"},{"type":"text","value":" here), and the adapter syncs the table options."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" directives ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderHeader"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderFooter"},{"type":"text","value":") render the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" definitions from your columns, whether they are plain values, templates, or components. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/flex-render","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FlexRender Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" and render context helpers."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" option is optional unless you use the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table Devtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The devtools identify tables by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":", and you register a table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTanStackTableDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the full "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/basic-inject-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic injectTable example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a runnable version with more columns and a footer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-a-feature-sorting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a Feature: Sorting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Features are opt-in in v9. To make columns sortable, register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSortingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" and the sorted row model in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", then wire the header click handler in the template."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// app.ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // enables sorting APIs and state\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // client-side sorting\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table',\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  sortIndicator(sortDirection: false | 'asc' | 'desc') {\n    if (sortDirection === 'asc') return ' 🔼'\n    if (sortDirection === 'desc') return ' 🔽'\n    return null\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- app.html: thead changes, tbody unchanged from above -->\n<thead>\n  @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n    <th>\n      @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n      <div\n        [style.cursor]=\"header.column.getCanSort() ? 'pointer' : null\"\n        (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\"\n      >\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        {{ sortIndicator(header.column.getIsSorted()) }}\n      </div>\n      }\n    </th>\n    }\n  </tr>\n  }\n</thead>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clicking a header now toggles between ascending, descending, and unsorted. Every other feature follows this same pattern: register the feature and its row model factory (when it has one) inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", then use the APIs it adds to the table, columns, and rows. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/sorting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/sorting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for custom sort functions, multi-sorting, and per-column options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to Go Next"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table state."}]},{"type":"text","value":" In v9, table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms, and table atoms are bridged to Angular signals for you. You usually do not need to manage state yourself. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" for starting values and call feature APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.setSorting(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.nextPage()"},{"type":"text","value":". When your app should own a state slice, or you want fine-grained subscriptions, read the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/table-state.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table State Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It is the foundational guide for everything else."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature guides."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each feature has its own guide, such as "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/column-filtering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Filtering"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/pagination.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/row-selection.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/column-visibility.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable tables."}]},{"type":"text","value":" When multiple tables in your app share features, row models, and component conventions, define them once with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/composable-tables.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full pattern, including pre-bound cell and header components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Browse the runnable "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/basic-inject-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular examples"}]},{"type":"text","value":", from basic tables to feature demos, to see intended usage end to end."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"your-first-table","text":"Your First Table","level":2},{"id":"add-a-feature-sorting","text":"Add a Feature: Sorting","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to Go Next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Table is a headless table library. It manages your table's state and logic (sorting, filtering, pagination, selection, and more) while you keep 100% control over the markup and styles. This page gets you from install to a rendering Angular table, then shows how to layer on your first feature.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-table\n```\n\n## Your First Table\n\nThe component and template below are complete. Drop them into an Angular app and you will see a working table.\n\n```ts\n// app.ts\nimport { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { FlexRender, injectTable, tableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// 1. Define the shape of your data\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}\n\n// 2. Create some data with a stable reference\nconst defaultData: Array<Person> = [\n  { firstName: 'tanner', lastName: 'linsley', age: 24 },\n  { firstName: 'tandy', lastName: 'miller', age: 40 },\n  { firstName: 'joe', lastName: 'dirte', age: 45 },\n]\n\n// 3. New in v9: declare which features this table uses (none yet)\nconst features = tableFeatures({})\n\n// 4. Define your columns\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = [\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'firstName', // accessorKey shorthand\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorFn: (row) => row.lastName, // accessorFn alternative with a custom id\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue<string>(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'age',\n    header: () => 'Age',\n  },\n]\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  imports: [FlexRender],\n  templateUrl: './app.html',\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n})\nexport class App {\n  // 5. Own the data with a signal so updates flow into the table\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  // 6. Create the table instance\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table', // registers this table with the devtools\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- app.html -->\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th>\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nA few things to note:\n\n- `tableFeatures({})` declares which optional features the table uses. Registering only what you need keeps bundles small and gives TypeScript accurate types for the table instance.\n- `injectTable` must be called in an injection context. Its initializer re-runs when Angular signals read inside it change (like `this.data()` here), and the adapter syncs the table options.\n- The `FlexRender` directives (`*flexRenderHeader`, `*flexRenderCell`, `*flexRenderFooter`) render the `header`, `cell`, and `footer` definitions from your columns, whether they are plain values, templates, or components. See the [FlexRender Guide](./guide/flex-render) for `flexRenderComponent` and render context helpers.\n- The `key` option is optional unless you use the [TanStack Table Devtools](../../devtools). The devtools identify tables by `key`, and you register a table with `injectTanStackTableDevtools` from `@tanstack/angular-table-devtools`.\n\nSee the full [Basic injectTable example](./examples/basic-inject-table) for a runnable version with more columns and a footer.\n\n## Add a Feature: Sorting\n\nFeatures are opt-in in v9. To make columns sortable, register `rowSortingFeature` and the sorted row model in `tableFeatures`, then wire the header click handler in the template.\n\n```ts\n// app.ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // enables sorting APIs and state\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // client-side sorting\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table',\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  sortIndicator(sortDirection: false | 'asc' | 'desc') {\n    if (sortDirection === 'asc') return ' 🔼'\n    if (sortDirection === 'desc') return ' 🔽'\n    return null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- app.html: thead changes, tbody unchanged from above -->\n<thead>\n  @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n    <th>\n      @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n      <div\n        [style.cursor]=\"header.column.getCanSort() ? 'pointer' : null\"\n        (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\"\n      >\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        {{ sortIndicator(header.column.getIsSorted()) }}\n      </div>\n      }\n    </th>\n    }\n  </tr>\n  }\n</thead>\n```\n\nClicking a header now toggles between ascending, descending, and unsorted. Every other feature follows this same pattern: register the feature and its row model factory (when it has one) inside `tableFeatures`, then use the APIs it adds to the table, columns, and rows. See the [Sorting Guide](./guide/sorting.md) and the [Sorting example](./examples/sorting) for custom sort functions, multi-sorting, and per-column options.\n\n## Where to Go Next\n\n**Table state.** In v9, table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms, and table atoms are bridged to Angular signals for you. You usually do not need to manage state yourself. Set `initialState` for starting values and call feature APIs like `table.setSorting(...)` or `table.nextPage()`. When your app should own a state slice, or you want fine-grained subscriptions, read the [Table State Guide](./guide/table-state.md). It is the foundational guide for everything else.\n\n**Feature guides.** Each feature has its own guide, such as [Column Filtering](./guide/column-filtering.md), [Pagination](./guide/pagination.md), [Row Selection](./guide/row-selection.md), and [Column Visibility](./guide/column-visibility.md).\n\n**Composable tables.** When multiple tables in your app share features, row models, and component conventions, define them once with `createTableHook`:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })\n```\n\nSee the [Composable Tables Guide](./guide/composable-tables.md) for the full pattern, including pre-bound cell and header components.\n\n**Examples.** Browse the runnable [Angular examples](./examples/basic-inject-table), from basic tables to feature demos, to see intended usage end to end.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nTanStack Table is a headless table library. It manages your table's state and logic (sorting, filtering, pagination, selection, and more) while you keep 100% control over the markup and styles. This page gets you from install to a rendering Angular table, then shows how to layer on your first feature.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-table\n```\n\n## Your First Table\n\nThe component and template below are complete. Drop them into an Angular app and you will see a working table.\n\n```ts\n// app.ts\nimport { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { FlexRender, injectTable, tableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// 1. Define the shape of your data\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n}\n\n// 2. Create some data with a stable reference\nconst defaultData: Array<Person> = [\n  { firstName: 'tanner', lastName: 'linsley', age: 24 },\n  { firstName: 'tandy', lastName: 'miller', age: 40 },\n  { firstName: 'joe', lastName: 'dirte', age: 45 },\n]\n\n// 3. New in v9: declare which features this table uses (none yet)\nconst features = tableFeatures({})\n\n// 4. Define your columns\nconst columns: Array<ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>> = [\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'firstName', // accessorKey shorthand\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorFn: (row) => row.lastName, // accessorFn alternative with a custom id\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue<string>(),\n  },\n  {\n    accessorKey: 'age',\n    header: () => 'Age',\n  },\n]\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  imports: [FlexRender],\n  templateUrl: './app.html',\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n})\nexport class App {\n  // 5. Own the data with a signal so updates flow into the table\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  // 6. Create the table instance\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table', // registers this table with the devtools\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- app.html -->\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n      <th>\n        @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        }\n      </th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getAllCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\">\n          {{ renderCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nA few things to note:\n\n- `tableFeatures({})` declares which optional features the table uses. Registering only what you need keeps bundles small and gives TypeScript accurate types for the table instance.\n- `injectTable` must be called in an injection context. Its initializer re-runs when Angular signals read inside it change (like `this.data()` here), and the adapter syncs the table options.\n- The `FlexRender` directives (`*flexRenderHeader`, `*flexRenderCell`, `*flexRenderFooter`) render the `header`, `cell`, and `footer` definitions from your columns, whether they are plain values, templates, or components. See the [FlexRender Guide](./guide/flex-render) for `flexRenderComponent` and render context helpers.\n- The `key` option is optional unless you use the [TanStack Table Devtools](../../devtools). The devtools identify tables by `key`, and you register a table with `injectTanStackTableDevtools` from `@tanstack/angular-table-devtools`.\n\nSee the full [Basic injectTable example](./examples/basic-inject-table) for a runnable version with more columns and a footer.\n\n## Add a Feature: Sorting\n\nFeatures are opt-in in v9. To make columns sortable, register `rowSortingFeature` and the sorted row model in `tableFeatures`, then wire the header click handler in the template.\n\n```ts\n// app.ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // enables sorting APIs and state\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // client-side sorting\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly data = signal<Array<Person>>([...defaultData])\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    key: 'person-table',\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  sortIndicator(sortDirection: false | 'asc' | 'desc') {\n    if (sortDirection === 'asc') return ' 🔼'\n    if (sortDirection === 'desc') return ' 🔽'\n    return null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- app.html: thead changes, tbody unchanged from above -->\n<thead>\n  @for (headerGroup of table.getHeaderGroups(); track headerGroup.id) {\n  <tr>\n    @for (header of headerGroup.headers; track header.id) {\n    <th>\n      @if (!header.isPlaceholder) {\n      <div\n        [style.cursor]=\"header.column.getCanSort() ? 'pointer' : null\"\n        (click)=\"header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()?.($event)\"\n      >\n        <ng-container *flexRenderHeader=\"header; let headerCell\">\n          {{ headerCell }}\n        </ng-container>\n        {{ sortIndicator(header.column.getIsSorted()) }}\n      </div>\n      }\n    </th>\n    }\n  </tr>\n  }\n</thead>\n```\n\nClicking a header now toggles between ascending, descending, and unsorted. Every other feature follows this same pattern: register the feature and its row model factory (when it has one) inside `tableFeatures`, then use the APIs it adds to the table, columns, and rows. See the [Sorting Guide](./guide/sorting.md) and the [Sorting example](./examples/sorting) for custom sort functions, multi-sorting, and per-column options.\n\n## Where to Go Next\n\n**Table state.** In v9, table state is backed by TanStack Store atoms, and table atoms are bridged to Angular signals for you. You usually do not need to manage state yourself. Set `initialState` for starting values and call feature APIs like `table.setSorting(...)` or `table.nextPage()`. When your app should own a state slice, or you want fine-grained subscriptions, read the [Table State Guide](./guide/table-state.md). It is the foundational guide for everything else.\n\n**Feature guides.** Each feature has its own guide, such as [Column Filtering](./guide/column-filtering.md), [Pagination](./guide/pagination.md), [Row Selection](./guide/row-selection.md), and [Column Visibility](./guide/column-visibility.md).\n\n**Composable tables.** When multiple tables in your app share features, row models, and component conventions, define them once with `createTableHook`:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })\n```\n\nSee the [Composable Tables Guide](./guide/composable-tables.md) for the full pattern, including pre-bound cell and header components.\n\n**Examples.** Browse the runnable [Angular examples](./examples/basic-inject-table), from basic tables to feature demos, to see intended usage end to end.\n"}
